From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Dedicated server mode: server-owned weather and time of day, admin login, player listing, activity log, window data

- relay: dedicated mode has no host; the server keeps the time of day (not the date) and the weather and broadcasts them,
  clients apply the weather wherever they are; admins log in with a password; console commands (players, kick, ban,
  weather, time, announce, help...); /who lists name, latency, address and location for admins (never in the public
  player list)
- relay logs what happens with a time: connections (with address), joins, refusals, leaving, losing connection and
  coming back, global chat, parties, trades, admin actions, weather changes and dropped messages once a minute
- relay.snapshot() gives a window the players, bans, sky and limits as plain data
- netlib.remoteAddress, server/server.lua, README, relay_test and server_test.py (runs the real server, terminal and
  window)

---
